==Maltese==
{{mt-root|s-b-t}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|mt|ar|سَبَّتَ}}, intensive of {{m|ar|سَبَتَ|t=to cut, smite, cast down}}. The root partly overlaps with {{ar-root|س ب ط|nocat=1}}, which could explain the Maltese ''a''-vocalism. It is likely that the verb was later associated with and influenced by the unrelated {{der|mt|scn|sbattiri}}, {{der|mt|it|sbattere}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|mt|/ˈsab.bat/}}

===Verb===
{{mt-verb|jsabbat}}

# to [[bang]], [[thump]], [[stamp]]

